  "worked_solution": "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-\\frac{3}{5}.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to (-3/5)}f(x)$ exists, and\n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{3}{5})={lim}_{x\\to (-3/5)}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {(-3/5)}^{-}}f(x)=7.\n$$",
